Alec Habig:
> Someone mentioned that they had found an off-by-one bug in the food code, that
> meant everything was less nutritous than it ought to be.  Is this one of the
> fixes in the upcoming patchlevel?

No, probably not.  Wait for patchlevel 2.

If you want a quick fix, here's an untested, one-line change to 3.1.0
that should ameliorate the problem.  (I haven't tested this because my
current working copy of eat.c is substantially different.  I'm trying
to fix several other food-related problems as well.)

I don't recommend using this fix.  It just makes your nethack
unnecessarily different from everyone else's.  Food isn't that big a
problem, is it?  The logfile I have shows two starvations out of 300
games.  (And one of the starvations was a stupid mistake, not due to
any real lack of food in the game.)

One game-playing tip: an easy way to get more food than you'll ever
need is to use a tinning kit on useless corpses, and toss the tins in
a polypile.  Given the dozens of wands of create monster you can find,
you can easily build up hundreds of food rations.  Certainly much more
than you can carry, even with a blessed bag of holding.

